type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Gangwon is a region on the east coast of the Korean Peninsula, crossed by the Taebaek Mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ganimi-kava"><span class="enc-name">Ganimi Kava</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Ganimi Kava is the Marathi term for the guerrilla tactics associated with Shivaji and the Maratha Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ganitasarasangraha"><span class="enc-name">Ganitasarasangraha</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ganitasarasangraha is a Sanskrit treatise on mathematics written about 850 by the Jain mathematician Mahaviracharya at the Rashtrakuta court of Amoghavarsha I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ganja-azerbaijan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ganja-azerbaijan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ganja, Azerbaijan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ganja is the second-largest city of Azerbaijan, in the west of the country.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ganjam-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ganjam-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ganjam district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ganjam is a coastal district of southern Odisha, India, centred on the city of Berhampur.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ganjifa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ganjifa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ganjifa</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Ganjifa is a family of card games played with round, hand-painted cards, introduced to India from Persia and popular at the Mughal court in the 